// r5_r6.zag — RT4 red-team reconstruction shim for the joke classifier's
// missing import r5_dispose(logic, ev). Reconstructed from the committed
// JOKEFIX_REPORT.md decision rule and observed run1 outputs:
//
//   g_classify sets: logic=2 if contra (contradiction fired);
//                    logic=1 if ev!=5 (satire/trope pattern, no contra);
//                    logic=0 if ev==5 (R_NO_PATTERN).
//   ev=3 (ns>=2, R_SATIRE), ev=2 (nt>=1, R_TROPE), ev=5 (no pattern).
// Decision rule (report): contradiction -> JOKING (R6 CONTRADICTS overrides);
//   SAT>=2 -> SATIRE; TROPE>=1 -> JOKING; else UNCERTAIN.
// Intent codes (report + run1): 2=JOKING (observed), 5=UNCERTAIN (observed);
//   3=SATIRE (only remaining natural code), 1=SINCERE/4=DECEPTIVE never emitted.
// Pipeline gate needs only: REJECT iff intent in {2,3}; WITHHOLD iff 5.
fn r5_dispose(logic:i32,ev:i32)i32{
    if(logic==2){return 2;}
    if(ev==3){return 3;}
    if(ev==2){return 2;}
    return 5;
}
